#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158482 :tutorial/content "There are two laws, called the **absorption laws**, that can be used to drastically simplify some logical expressions.\n\n- The law that conjunction absorbs disjunction is stated as $$A \\land (A \\lor B) \\equiv A.$$\n- Likewise, the law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as $$A \\lor (A \\land B) \\equiv A.$$\n\nSometimes, the laws are stated more concisely as\n\n$$A \\land (A \\lor B) \\equiv A \\lor (A \\land B) \\equiv A.$$\n\nTo prove that these laws hold, we can construct truth tables:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\, A \\land (A \\lor B) \\,$ | $\\, A \\lor (A \\land B) \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |" :tutorial/id #uuid "dcc7f471-b2da-52b6-b003-76ae7ca1e64a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4344 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
